{"title":"2001 JBMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9e702326a58a2848df8758e667ae40abdbfb150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle C = 90^\\circ$\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b49e824f35a5f63de9c462efdccdabfd8e1400.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA \\ne CB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/e/20e8e26d580012b86d8fe55e70e5740908c35af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CH$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> be an altitude and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/2/4d21d821b4d355d89a283fb4770140d1497d26c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CL$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> be an interior angle bisector.  Show that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/516347f8d3b28b18096a75c16e7fd7310cd14f16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X \\ne C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> on the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/d/3dda116148cf63a5139291b72ac7723a8bb7afb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CL,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"16\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/1/cd17d43e4a12224fcc9fcda8427a74f92fe5c68f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle XAC \\ne \\angle XBC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"17\" />.  Also show that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/1/dc1ab97e5eba9e5798ad9f42577bdcd806262f0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y \\ne C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" /> on the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/e/20e8e26d580012b86d8fe55e70e5740908c35af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CH$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/9/5594c182004855d8ce1915687a482f1fd07a8aaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle YAC \\ne \\angle YBC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/a/72a7f29e9eaf8d3bfb88d3969df78cfd9319e3c4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(30,0)--(0,40)--(0,0)); dot((0,0)); label(&quot;C&quot;,(0,0),SW); dot((0,40)); label(&quot;A&quot;,(0,40),NW); dot((30,0)); label(&quot;B&quot;,(30,0),SE);  draw((0,0)--(120/7,120/7)); dot((120/7,120/7)); label(&quot;L&quot;,(120/7,120/7),NE);  dot((10,10)); label(&quot;X&quot;,(10,10),S); draw((0,40)--(10,10)--(30,0));  draw(anglemark((0,0),(0,40),(10,10),150)); draw(anglemark((10,10),(30,0),(0,0),150)); [/asy]\" width=\"202\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>Assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/e/e8e6f6cf735444b195167e7df05300b2750ad3ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle XAC = \\angle XBC$\" width=\"139\" height=\"13\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/2/4d21d821b4d355d89a283fb4770140d1497d26c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CL$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_bisector\" title=\"Angle bisector\">angle bisector</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/3/fd3dfac5859d0d9ea1dd6189e46c786144ce1c3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/e/40e19817470188de26cec3be003057dc9e649254.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACX = \\angle BCX.$\" width=\"142\" height=\"13\" />  Thus, by AAS Congruency, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/a/e4a00e0db38dc2eaa1d763d8c30f12c1fbb61e66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACX \\cong \\triangle BCX,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"149\" height=\"17\" /> which results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/1/ae1c97d4d65b99ec000470a437414dad2caae11d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = BC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" />  But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/6/ba6d8fa604ea292c5152c7d18460269daa10909b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC \\ne BC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"17\" /> so by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Proof_by_contradiction\" title=\"Proof by contradiction\">proof by contradiction</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/0/a50785b57b40e1a6a1660f22f3fd01e68a19ba49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle XAC \\ne \\angle XBC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/2/f12a5b0d06601be8766fb4567b424adfbce720e0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(30,0)--(0,40)--(0,0)); dot((0,0)); label(&quot;C&quot;,(0,0),SW); dot((0,40)); label(&quot;A&quot;,(0,40),NW); dot((30,0)); label(&quot;B&quot;,(30,0),SE);  draw((0,0)--(96/5,72/5)); dot((96/5,72/5)); label(&quot;H&quot;,(96/5,72/5),NE);  dot((12,9)); label(&quot;Y&quot;,(12,9),NW); draw((0,40)--(12,9)--(30,0)); draw((0,9)--(12,9)--(12,0),dotted);  dot((0,9)); label(&quot;$A&#39;$&quot;,(0,9),W); dot((12,0)); label(&quot;$B&#39;$&quot;,(12,0),S);  draw(anglemark((0,0),(0,40),(12,9),150)); draw(anglemark((0,0),(0,40),(12,9),200)); draw(anglemark((12,9),(30,0),(0,0),150)); draw(anglemark((12,9),(30,0),(0,0),200));  [/asy]\" width=\"205\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>Assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/4/6d4fb221b05bff77966cd16e608fc02be692e9c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle YAC = \\angle YBC$\" width=\"135\" height=\"13\" />.  Draw points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> respectively such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/b/44b3f3aaea4269215bafa5652c783b0dad241b4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AY&#39;BC$\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> is a rectangle.  That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/3/c13359c51e44adb16de8aead92cf167fe45ec0c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;BHY$\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/8/b082a38749d11522560f0e98928543d870315f44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA&#39;YH$\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cyclic_quadrilaterals\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Cyclic quadrilaterals\">cyclic quadrilaterals</a>, which means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/5/cc575df212389a3a7f1fc9f3645db23fb015151d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A&#39;HY = \\angle B&#39;HY.$\" width=\"150\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/3/4e39919f572d9421d9fe01d80321554dfafdeced.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;B&#39;$\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> is bisected by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/b/bcb82bca7de59684e050803ba493e050e355614f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HC$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" />, by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_Bisector_Theorem\" title=\"Angle Bisector Theorem\">Angle Bisector Theorem</a>, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/5/275dbbb0d908ffba45225cbe38b870e18f91fc03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HA&#39; = HB&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" /> so by SAS Congruency, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb379d122e5fce962c41bfafbb87e78e32b918c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle HA&#39;Y \\cong \\triangle HB&#39;Y,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"157\" height=\"17\" /> making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/9/8e9043ebce79ca9e63ad7f68588d065fe1eaa04c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;Y = YB&#39;$\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/4/42426918f5577719e6191f1402fed912033f9c60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;YCB&#39;$\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" /> a square.  This also means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/8/c98005e5ce61357fdbadeeb0f593ceaf63883b55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A&#39;CY = \\angle B&#39;CY,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"146\" height=\"17\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/4/cf441c32196fe2d613ff893f30d3c72d2b3924cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACY \\cong \\triangle BCY$\" width=\"142\" height=\"13\" /> by AAS Congruency, making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/1/ae1c97d4d65b99ec000470a437414dad2caae11d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = BC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" />  However, it is given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/6/ba6d8fa604ea292c5152c7d18460269daa10909b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC \\ne BC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"17\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/9/5594c182004855d8ce1915687a482f1fd07a8aaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle YAC \\ne \\angle YBC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"17\" /> by proof by contradiction.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO\" title=\"2001 JBMO\">2001 JBMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems\" title=\"2001 JBMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13_contests\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 JBMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 JBMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 JBMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 JBMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 JBMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JBMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" title=\"JBMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\"> All JBMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017195413\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.037 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 246/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 868/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 36/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8150/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.780      1 Template:JBMO_box\n100.00%    6.780      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16648:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017195413 and revision id 97222. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}